Task: make the data-safety guardrails (added in 8825b41) never break a normal run, and fix B22
(IAM MalformedPolicyDocument on setup).

B22: iam/glue.json had a "_comment" INSIDE a Policy Statement (plus three doc-level "_comment"
keys); IAM rejects put-role-policy with MalformedPolicyDocument, so every setup failed. Removed
them (explanations moved to docs/IAM_POLICY_NOTES.md); tools/setup.sh split_iam and the
MANUAL_SETUP fill-in step now strip any non-IAM key from TrustPolicy/Policy/VpcPolicy (and their
Statements) before put-role-policy as a backstop. New tests/test_iam_policies.py asserts every
Statement in iam/*.json carries only valid IAM keys and that both strip backstops work.

Ease guardrails (principle: a guard may only STOP a destructive action; it must NEVER fail a run
for its own bookkeeping — a missing permission, missing control table, a lock it can't take, or a
check it can't compute):
- New master setting guardrails_mode = warn (default) | strict, plumbed params.csv -> pipeline.json
  -> resolve_task -> create_glue_jobs -> load/validate/CDC job args, with per-guard knobs
  cdc_file_order_action (G8), cdc_nopk_overmatch_action (G7), validate_count_check /
  cutover_count_check (G10). strict restores fail-closed.
- HARD G1/G4/G6 still refuse the destructive op (and only that op; the per-table loop keeps the run
  going). SOFT G2/G3/G5/G7/G8/G9/G10 warn + continue by default; each guard call is wrapped so an
  exception can't raise into the main path.
- G2 missing states:DescribeExecution no longer fails a reblank; G3 warns+proceeds on a bookkeeping
  lock failure and skips only on a live holder; G7/G8 warn+apply; G10 mismatch is a WARNING and
  validate/cutover still pass. All reversible via guardrails_mode=strict or the per-guard setting.
- New control bookkeeping (cdc_control_lock, audit_log, cdc_status counters) is add-if-missing (no
  DEFAULT-on-ALTER, B17-safe); a create/upgrade failure warns and continues.
- Shared CDC helpers (incl. new guard_action_blocks / emit_guard_warn_metric) stay byte-identical
  across the continuous + composite engines.

