Task: fix B23 — startup `ForkCdcStartNotConfirmed` was a FALSE failure for every composite (ck)
and big-table (bg) CDC fork. The workflow polled the start marker at the TASK-level key
config/_task/<suffix>/_cdc_started/<exec>-ck-<slug>.json, but each fork CDC job runs with
--config_prefix = its FORK prefix (.../_orchestrator/ck-<slug>/ or .../_orchestrator/bg-<slug>/)
and write_started_marker() writes under <CONFIG_PREFIX>_cdc_started/. The poll never matched, the
Map waited 45 min and failed, while the fork CDC job was actually RUNNING. Main CDC was fine (its
config_prefix IS the task prefix).

Fix:
- plan_split.py now emits config_prefix_key (bare S3 key, trailing slash) for every ck and bg fork.
- startup.asl.json CheckForkStarted now polls the fork's OWN prefix:
  States.Format('{}_cdc_started/{}-ck-{}.json', $.config_prefix_key, $.execName, $.fork_slug).
- Both CDC scripts (glue_cdc_composite.py, glue_cdc_continuous.py) ALSO write a second copy of the
  start marker at the task level when --cdc_owners_key is present (its dirname is the task prefix),
  so older/unpatched workflows confirm too. Main run still writes once.
- Optional _latest.json LastModified fallback: deliberately not added (not simpler; the two fixes
  above are deterministic and cover back-compat).

Both fork kinds confirmed affected and fixed (ck + bg exercised in the new test).

